{:edb/db-before-t 2722 :edb/db-after-t 2723 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536035 50 #inst "2026-10-09T13:20:38.218Z" 13194139536035 true] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380391 13194139536035 true] [17592186124557 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380398 13194139536035 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380377 13194139536035 true] [17592186124558 1020 #edb/ref 17592186380384 13194139536035 true] [17592186124726 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536035 true] [17592186124726 1100 "Find the domain of the function $f(x, y) = e^{x^{2} - y^{2}}$." 13194139536035 false] [17592186124726 1100 "Find the domain of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}.$" 13194139536035 true] [17592186124726 1145 "Notice that\n\n- ${x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ is defined for all $x$ and $y,$ and\n\n- ${e}^{g(x,y)}$ is defined if $g(x,y)$ is defined.\n\nAs a result, ${e}^{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is defined for all values of $x$ and $y.$ This means that the domain of $f$ is the entire $xy$-plane." 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380378 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1089 "q-158192" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1100 "Which of the following shaded regions corresponds to the domain of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}?$" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1113 #uuid "d9d58fba-c75c-5614-b1bd-365ad3c734ff" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380377 1145 "The function is well-defined at all points $(x,y)$ for which the following condition is satisfied:\n\n- The expression under the square root is non-negative, and\n\n- the expression in the denominator is not equal to zero.\n\nAs a result, the points in the domain must satisfy the following inequalities:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}>0\\,⟹\\,{y}^{2}<{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,-|x|<y<|x|\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,-|x|<y<|x|}.\n$$\n\nSince the inequality involves the $<$ sign, the curves are *not* part of the domain. Therefore, we draw the dashed lines $y=-|x|$ and $y=|x|,$ and shade the area *below* the curve $y=|x|,$ and *above* the curve $y=-|x|.$\n\nThe resulting domain is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/c06082999e1737b6e4ea5d32a3d8d77a271e3db49c38cc3725422bcb979676d0.png)" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380379 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380380 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380381 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380382 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380383 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1041 "selection" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380381 13194139536035 true] [17592186380378 1110 #uuid "5ec9f70a-3be4-5eea-89f1-33008c5591d6" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380379 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/a40b0a38c8a1a6c9975e13b23db60e583d60e3b8813a4faa3f923ecfdd515cd5.png" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536035 true] [17592186380379 1111 #uuid "8fcc67b7-6a4d-550c-b6b0-d74817b242e8" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380380 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/a11d5693c185fde49044feb92d615f5bf3496735c02e4f373e0ffa40111cc964.png" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139536035 true] [17592186380380 1111 #uuid "aa4778b3-e05d-5ad9-b348-b89b2d5fe8ea" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380381 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074200/assets/6727002ca8a7ee3451f09e239f49693ec6819053525c8fbe4ce5749fd8622254.png" 13194139536035 true] [17592186380381 1103 #edb/ref 1759